                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> Oh, you are too fast hahaha I accidently posted without properly finishing it.\r\n\r\nYou gave the necessary title, that was enough :sweat_smile:\r\n\r\nThe buffer-local variable having three valuable states (`nil`, `false`, `true`) instead of two (false-ish `nil`+`false` and `true`) is one of the main reasons why I am hesitant to implement this kind of behavior (as mentioned in linked comment).\r\n\r\n> I suggested this, because I particularly would like indentscope to be disabled by default, and enable only on buffers that I want, so I disable it globally after `setup()` and would change the buffer flag on the buffers I want using a command or keymap.\r\n\r\nThe suggested way to achieve this is to [automatically set buffer-local variable to `true`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0429e9ee9d35faef51971abdbb1b26d2540b5a5f/doc/mini.txt#L349-L355) and set it to `false` when want to enable it.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Oh, you are too fast hahaha I accidently posted without properly finishing it.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">You gave the necessary title, that was enough 😅</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The buffer-local variable having three valuable states (<code class=\"notranslate\">nil</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code>) instead of two (false-ish <code class=\"notranslate\">nil</code>+<code class=\"notranslate\">false</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code>) is one of the main reasons why I am hesitant to implement this kind of behavior (as mentioned in linked comment).</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I suggested this, because I particularly would like indentscope to be disabled by default, and enable only on buffers that I want, so I disable it globally after <code class=\"notranslate\">setup()</code> and would change the buffer flag on the buffers I want using a command or keymap.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The suggested way to achieve this is to <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0429e9ee9d35faef51971abdbb1b26d2540b5a5f/doc/mini.txt#L349-L355\">automatically set buffer-local variable to <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code></a> and set it to <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code> when want to enable it.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Oh, you are too fast hahaha I accidently posted without properly finishing it.\n\nYou gave the necessary title, that was enough 😅\nThe buffer-local variable having three valuable states (nil, false, true) instead of two (false-ish nil+false and true) is one of the main reasons why I am hesitant to implement this kind of behavior (as mentioned in linked comment).\n\nI suggested this, because I particularly would like indentscope to be disabled by default, and enable only on buffers that I want, so I disable it globally after setup() and would change the buffer flag on the buffers I want using a command or keymap.\n\nThe suggested way to achieve this is to automatically set buffer-local variable to true and set it to false when want to enable it.",
